{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "01PD", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{O}$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:329d559bd06077acab0ca13d14ea00c4977c01ff8d871fadd9f8e68c6ff386bd", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:7f70c99ece826d2b9ebc03ae2a6482e818311cc7d1b2d00ec060358a55dec7f8", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThe following lemma says that every quasi-coherent sheaf on a quasi-compact\nand quasi-separated scheme is a filtered colimit of <MATH_0001>-modules\nof finite presentation. Actually, we reformulate this in (perhaps more\nfamiliar) terms of directed colimits over directed sets in the next lemma.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:3e0f0aee1793be5bdd6b0ea8ae0b0415b4ffa1e56a9d3e335fbaff9726d0e256", "unit_id": "tag:01PD:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "properties", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01PD", "placeholders": {"LOCKED_0001": "\\begin{slogan}\nQuasi-coherent modules on quasi-compact and quasi-separated schemes\nare filtered colimits of finitely presented modules.\n\\end{slogan}", "MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$X$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{O}_X$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{I}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{I} \\to \\textit{Mod}(\\mathcal{O}_X)$", "MATH_0007": "$i \\mapsto \\mathcal{F}_i$", "MATH_0008": "$\\mathcal{O}_X$", "MATH_0009": "$\\varphi_i : \\mathcal{F}_i \\to \\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0010": "$\\mathcal{F}_i$", "MATH_0011": "$\\varphi_i$", "MATH_0012": "$$\n\\colim_i \\mathcal{F}_i\n=\n\\mathcal{F}.\n$$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{categories-definition-directed}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{categories-section-limits}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-directed-colimit-diagram-finite-presentation}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:32cc277223585ac5d8efc7077c923c6411ff3dc9eed2122d4bf1b3de47cb1baa", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:c9e006b8b110aa449645f907994e6ed54b155434e090cc36147ecda6a41ef0fc", "source_text": "<LOCKED_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a scheme. Assume <MATH_0002> is quasi-compact and quasi-separated.\nLet <MATH_0003> be a quasi-coherent <MATH_0004>-module.\nThere exist\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> a filtered index category <MATH_0005> (see\nCategories, Definition <REF_0001>),\n<STRUCT_0003> a diagram <MATH_0006> (see\nCategories, Section <REF_0002>),\n<MATH_0007>,\n<STRUCT_0004> morphisms of <MATH_0008>-modules\n<MATH_0009>\n<STRUCT_0005>\nsuch that each <MATH_0010> is of finite presentation\nand such that the morphisms <MATH_0011> induce an